course: dictionary
lesson: 1190
title: One word, many meanings: brush
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brush is a word with more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Most often it is a tool with bristles, but it can also be an action: «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush, because hard scrubbing hurts the gums.» Here brushed is something you do, and brush is the thing you use.
explain: Look for clues. «Her hand brushed mine» does not mean cleaned or painted. The word brushed describes touching lightly while passing, because the hands are touching, not scrubbing. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are harder to spot. Brush can also mean low bushes and small trees, the scrub in dry land, and a brush fire is a bushfire. Brush up on something means to practise it again, so if someone says they need to brush up on their spelling, they are going to practise it.
fact: A brush is a tool with many bristles on a handle.
fact: As a verb, brush means to clean or tidy with a brush, as in brush your teeth or brush your hair.
fact: To brush against something means to touch it lightly while passing.
fact: Brush up on means to practise something again.
fact: Brush can mean low bushes and small trees, and a brush fire is a fire in dry bush land.
exercise: «Broken glass is swept up carefully with a brush and dustpan.» What is a brush in this sentence? | A small wild bush | A way of touching lightly | A type of paint | *A tool with bristles for sweeping
exercise: «Her hand brushed mine.» What does brushed mean here? | Tangled together | Painted over | *Touched lightly while passing | Cleaned with bristles
exercise: Ella says she needs to brush up on her times tables. What does brush up on mean? | To paint over a mistake | *To practise something again | To cut something short | To wash something off
test: «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush, because hard scrubbing hurts the gums and wears the teeth.» Why should you brush gently? | *So you do not hurt the gums or wear the teeth | Because soft brushes are the only kind that work | So the brush lasts for one day only | So the toothpaste dries faster
test: What is a brush fire? | A fire lit with a paintbrush | A fire put out with a hairbrush | *A fire in dry bush land | A fire that lights up when you brush your teeth
exam: The children brush their teeth twice a day. Which word in this sentence is the verb? | teeth | twice | *brush | children
